    → PK is (created_at, vehicle_id, signal) — already provides unique constraint

=== REASONING ===
Problem: During rolling deploys, two pods subscribe to the same MQTT topic.
Both receive the same signal and INSERT into signal_log. If their NOW() calls
differ by microseconds, both rows insert — causing SUM/AVG double-counting.

Solution (two layers):
1. In-memory dedup: Before batch insert, dedup rows with the same
   (vehicle_id, signal, Unix-second timestamp). Last value wins. This prevents
   most duplicate INSERTs from reaching the DB at all.
2. ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING: Replace CopyFrom (which cannot express ON CONFLICT)
   with pgx.Batch of individual INSERT statements using
   ON CONFLICT (created_at, vehicle_id, signal) DO NOTHING.
   pgx.SendBatch pipelines all queries in a single round-trip — efficient.
3. MQTT comment: Added documentation about MQTT v5 shared subscriptions
   ($share/teslasync/...) as a future upgrade path to eliminate duplicates
   at the broker level.

No new migration needed — PK from prompt 00 already serves as unique constraint.

=== CHANGES ===
1. internal/database/signal_history_writer.go
   - Added in-memory dedup map before batch insert (lines 130-145)
   - Replaced CopyFrom with pgx.Batch + INSERT ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING (lines 147-167)

2. internal/mqtt/subscriber.go
   - Added comment block near Subscribe() explaining duplicate delivery during
     rolling deploys and the MQTT v5 shared subscription upgrade path (lines 76-85)

